---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Barrier Frustration Training San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Break the cycle of frustration at fences, windows, and crates. We teach your dog impulse control and neutrality in San Jacinto using a balanced approach.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Barrier Frustration Training",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/barrier-frustration"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/leash-reactivity-bootcamp" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Leash Reactivity Bootcamp</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Barrier Frustration</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Barrier Frustration Training in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If your dog acts like a maniac the second a fence, window, or crate door comes between them and the world, you’re dealing with barrier frustration. It’s that explosion of chaos where a "nice" dog turns into a snarling mess because they can’t get to the mailman.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These outbursts are symptoms of a total lack of impulse control and spatial boundaries. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or hand out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to see the interaction at your fence or window before we can build a plan. Yelling "Quiet!" usually does nothing once the adrenaline hits—your dog has already checked out and needs real guidance.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Breaking the Cycle of Frustration
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Barrier frustration isn't always about "aggression"—it’s a total lack of impulse control. For 8 years, I’ve specialized in teaching dogs that the fence or the window isn't a cue to lose their minds. My balanced approach uses high-value rewards to mark "quiet" choices, but I also use calibrated leash corrections. We have to interrupt the hyper-fixation before it escalates. If you can't break the stare, you can't change the behavior.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I often use my helper dog, Rocky, for these sessions. Rocky is my "Neutral Presence." He can walk past a barking dog or a frantic fence-fighter without reacting. By having your dog watch Rocky’s indifference, we show them that they can also choose to be neutral. We provide the clarity that other dogs exist in the world, and we have to find a way to live with them without constant conflict.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We bring the training to the source—your home, your gate, or the local distraction. We work around San Jacinto, from delivery truck routes to busy residential areas near the Ramona Expressway. My goal is to create a "neutral" dog that can watch the world go by from your porch without feeling the need to scream at it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Stop letting your dog's fence-fighting define your relationship with the neighborhood. Let’s build some impulse control.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
